  "raw": {
    "https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut": {
      "title": "Working",
      "description": "Working at AUT - AUT We value your privacy We use cookies to enhance your browsing experience, enable features like live chat and embedded media, serve personalised ads and content, and understand how our website is used. By clicking “Accept All”, you consent to our use of cookies. Cookie Policy Customise Reject All Accept All Customise Consent Preferences We use cookies to help you navigate efficiently and perform certain functions. You will find detailed information about all cookies under each consent category below. The cookies that are categorised as \"Necessary\" are stored on your browser as they are essential for enabling the basic functionalities of the site. ... Show more For more information on how Google's third-party cookies operate and handle your data, see: Google Privacy Policy Necessary Always Active Necessary cookies are required to enable the basic features of this site, such as providing secure log-in or adjusting your consent preferences. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable data. Cookie dxp-sessionid Duration 1 hour Description Maintains the user's session within the Squiz DXP platform. Required for navigation, form interactions, and core site functionality. Cookie SQ_SYSTEM_SESSION Duration session Description Session cookie used by the Squiz CMS to track authenticated sessions and preserve user state across pages. Essential for system functions such as logins and editing tools. Cookie __cf_bm Duration 1 hour Description This cookie, set by Cloudflare, is used to support Cloudflare Bot Management. Cookie li_gc Duration 6 months Description Linkedin set this cookie for storing visitor's consent regarding using cookies for non-essential purposes. Cookie AWSALBCORS Duration 7 days Description Amazon Web Services set this cookie for load balancing. Cookie cookieyes-consent Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description CookieYes sets this cookie to remember users' consent preferences so that their preferences are respected on subsequent visits to this site. It does not collect or store any personal information about the site visitors. Functional Functional cookies help perform certain functionalities like sharing the content of the website on social media platforms, collecting feedback, and other third-party features. Cookie theme Duration session Description This cookie is used to set the colour theme of the website. Cookie lidc Duration 1 day Description LinkedIn sets the lidc cookie to facilitate data center selection. Analytics Analytical cookies are used to understand how visitors interact with the website. These cookies help provide information on metrics such as the number of visitors, bounce rate, traffic source, etc. Cookie gtm-session-start Duration 1 hour Description Records the start time of a user session for Google Tag Manager. Used to help measure website usage and session duration. Cookie _ga Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to calculate visitor, session and campaign data and track site usage for the site's analytics report. The cookie stores information anonymously and assigns a randomly generated number to recognise unique visitors. Cookie _gid Duration 1 day Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store information on how visitors use a website while also creating an analytics report of the website's performance. Some of the collected data includes the number of visitors, their source, and the pages they visit anonymously. Cookie _gat_UA-* Duration 1 minute Description Google Analytics sets this cookie for user behaviour tracking. Cookie _ga_* Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store and count page views. Cookie _hjSessionUser_* Duration 1 year Description Hotjar sets this cookie to ensure data from subsequent visits to the same site is attributed to the same user ID, which persists in the Hotjar User ID, which is unique to that site. Cookie _hjSession_* Duration 1 hour Description Hotjar sets this cookie to ensure data from subsequent visits to the same site is attributed to the same user ID, which persists in the Hotjar User ID, which is unique to that site. Cookie _twpid Duration 1 year 24 days Description This cookie is set by Tealium to assign a unique, anonymous identifier to each visitor. It allows the platform to recognise the same user across different sessions and domains to provide a consistent experience, support visitor stitching for unified profiles, and generate accurate website usage statistics. Performance Performance cookies are used to understand and analyse the key performance indexes of the website which helps in delivering a better user experience for the visitors. Cookie AWSALB Duration 7 days Description AWSALB is an application load balancer cookie set by Amazon Web Services to map the session to the target. Advertisement Advertisement cookies are used to provide visitors with customised advertisements based on the pages you visited previously and to analyse the effectiveness of the ad campaigns. Cookie ttcsid_C5N07UH1P6O5QGAPR6KG Duration 3 months Description TikTok Pixel session identifier used for analytics, ad attribution, and measuring campaign performance. Cookie ttcsid Duration 3 months Description Tracks user behaviour for TikTok advertising, enabling ad performance measurement and personalised marketing. Cookie pageviewCount Duration session Description This cookie is used for determining the number of pages visited by a visitor on the website. It is used for marketing purposes. Cookie _ttp Duration 3 months Description TikTok set this cookie to track and improve the performance of advertising campaigns, as well as to personalise the user experience. Cookie muc_ads Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Twitter sets this cookie to collect user behaviour and interaction data to optimize the website. Cookie personalization_id Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Twitter sets this cookie to integrate and share features for social media and also store information about how the user uses the website, for tracking and targeting. Cookie _mkto_trk Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description This cookie, provided by Marketo, has information (such as a unique user ID) that is used to track the user's site usage. The cookies set by Marketo are readable only by Marketo. Cookie bcookie Duration 1 year Description LinkedIn sets this cookie from LinkedIn share buttons and ad tags to recognize browser IDs. Cookie _tt_enable_cookie Duration 3 months Description Tiktok set this cookie to collect data about behaviour and activities on the website and to measure the effectiveness of the advertising. Cookie _gcl_au Duration 3 months Description Google Tag Manager sets this cookie to experiment advertisement efficiency of websites using their services. Uncategorised Other uncategorised cookies are those that are being analysed and have not been classified into a category as yet. No cookies to display. Reject All Save My Preferences Accept All Skip to Content Skip to Main navigation Top bar navigation Students Staff Alumni Enquire Apply Website search Main navigation AUT Website search Toggle navigation Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Enquire Apply Students Staff Alumni Ako Study Ako Study Ready to plan for a future you're confident about? Explore programmes that lead to real careers, find your perfect fit and make your next move count. Find out more Study options Why study at AUT? Applying Entry requirements Fees and scholarships Changing my enrolment Information for high school students Information for career advisors Information for parents and whānau Information for adult learners Semester dates University that works differently Why study at AUT? See why we do things differently here at AUT and what that means for your learning. Learn more Tāwāhi International Tāwāhi International Thinking of studying in New Zealand? See why students from over 140 countries choose AUT for modern learning experiences that prepare you for success. Find out more Study options for international students Why study at AUT as an international student Scholarships for international students International student support Check before you come to New Zealand Meet AUT in your country International agents Contact us AUT International Office AUT China Website - 奥克兰理工大学中文官方网站 Scholarships for international students International student support Worried about the cost of studying in New Zealand? There's funding available – and you might qualify. Learn more Oranga Tauira Student Life Oranga Tauira Student Life We've got your back from day one. Discover all the support and experiences that help you feel at home and make the most of every uni moment. Find out more New students Around campus Accommodation Studying & IT Support services Student health and wellbeing Opportunities & careers Graduation Life in Auckland AUTSA - AUT student association We've got your back Financial services and support for students Facing financial challenges? We're here to help with essential support when you need it most. Learn more Rangahau Research Rangahau Research Problems that keep communities up at night? We're working on those. Explore research that creates solutions for real-world challenges that matter well beyond the university. Find out more Research networks, institutes and centres AUT Ventures (research commercialisation) Research and development services Participate in AUT research Research Week AUT Research Office Faculty postgraduate contacts Academic departments Graduate Research School Postgraduate research student support Postgraduate study options Research ethics Research that matters Research networks, institutes and centres From AI to public health, our research networks, institutes and centres work on problems that really matter. Learn more Ngātahi Partnerships Ngātahi Partnerships Ready to solve problems together? Discover how we partner with industry, community and government to tackle real challenges and drive meaningful change together. Learn  more Employ a student or graduate: find AUT talent for your business Research and development services Promote your business on campus: employer and industry events Use AUT's research facilities and equipment AUT Ventures (research commercialisation) Auckland FC partnership Community that cares Student Support Fund When students need support, our community steps up. See how you can help make a difference. Learn more Mō Mātou About Mō Mātou About Curious about AUT? Get to know our story, meet our leadership and find out what makes us different as a top modern university. Find out more AUT’s leadership Faculties and schools Campuses and locations Teaching, learning and assessment AUT rankings AUT awards and honours AI at AUT Sustainability Disability Action Plan Māori at AUT Pacific at AUT Working at AUT AUT values Our facilities Check a graduate’s qualification AUT Impact Policy hub History of AUT Contact AUT Apply Website search Home About Working at AUT Working at AUT Browse jobs Get job alerts AUT is where curious, driven people come to do work that matters. Teaching that inspires. Research that lands in the world. Professional expertise that keeps a great university moving forward. AUT is led by people who back good ideas wherever they come from. Our strategy, Te Kete, sets a clear direction – and whatever your role, you're part of delivering it. Our values – pono, tika and aroha – aren't just on a poster. You feel them in how decisions get made, in how people show up for each other, and in work fuelled by real purpose. Previous Not sure what a career at AUT actually looks like? Watch this. What does University Librarian Kim Tairi love about AUT? Watch this. What does Dr Mike Frecklington, Head of Podiatry, love about AUT? Watch this. Next For academics If you want to teach with purpose and see your research make a real difference, AUT is built for that. Teaching is valued as highly as research output, and you'll have the freedom to build work that matters. Academic careers at AUT For professional staff At AUT, professional staff keep a complex, forward-looking university running well – and moving forward. If you want your work to connect directly to something that matters, this is the right place. Professional careers at AUT Temps on Campus Need flexible work in Auckland? Temps on Campus connects skilled people with short-term roles across AUT – from administration and events to technical and student-facing work. Temps on Campus What’s it like to work at AUT Get to know AUT Three campuses, 27,000+ students, world-ranked research. Find out what kind of university AUT is before you apply. Get to know AUT Staff benefits Free study, generous leave, flexible working and more. Find out what AUT offers the people who work here. Staff benefits Embracing diversity and inclusion More than half our staff were born overseas. Find out how AUT builds a workplace where everyone belongs. Diversity and inclusion Join a community where you belong and thrive Find out how AUT supports Māori and Pacific staff, and what belonging looks like here. Māori and Pacific staff Job application and interview process Knowing what to expect makes for a better application. Here's how AUT's recruitment process works. Recruitment process Living and working in Auckland Relocating? Find out what life in Auckland actually looks like – and why so many people who come to work at AUT find it's a place they want to stay. Living in Auckland AUT gives me the freedom to be open, candid, and creative in my research and teaching while still being part of something larger. What has surprised me most is the way AUT is unapologetically different to other universities. We've carved out our own niche. AUT provides the space and support to pursue ambitious ideas, and the people around you want to see those ideas come to life. AUT has given me the opportunity to grow, contribute and be part of something bigger than myself – and that’s what has kept me here. Every day, I see staff across the university go above and beyond for students. The level of care and commitment is inspiring. For an organisation as large as ours, we can easily find opportunities to connect with one another, irrespective of any roles or positions we hold. AUT is a young and agile university, and I feel like we all help shape its direction. I’ve been able to build authentic relationships with people willing to listen, support and help create change together. Rather than teaching, researching and engaging with industry as separate activities, AUT has created an environment where they all reinforce one another. What has surprised me most is the extent to which AUT has established itself as a leader in the social impact space. AUT has supported my growth, encouraged continuous learning and provided the chance to work with colleagues who genuinely care about students and each other. I can see the immediate impact our work has on university students' lives, which I never really got in corporate consulting. Dr Amy Errmann Senior Lecturer, Marketing & International Business Helen Rayner Senior Manager – Planning and Performance, Strategy and Planning Associate Professor Benjamin Dehe Deputy Head, Department of Management, Technology and Organisation Andy Feau Student Transition and Retention Senior Manager, Student Hub Peter Shimwell Director Student Counselling & Health Dr Rufus McEwan Associate Head of School, Communication Studies Associate Professor Adrian Schoone Head of School, Education Tash Puketapu Kaiurungi, People & Culture Dr Sarah Wymer Senior Lecturer, Sport Leadership and Management Associate Professor Syrus Islam Associate Professor & Leader of the AUT Accounting for Social Impact Research Group, Accounting Helen HuiQun Xue School Registrar, Future Environments Alex Hiramatsu Senior Technology Project Manager, AI Acceleration Centre VIEW ALL Previous Next Get in touch Have a question about a specific role? Contact the recruitment consultant named in the listing. For everything else, our People and Culture team is here: Phone: +64 9 921 9499 Hours: 9am to 5pm, Monday to Friday CONTACT US ONLINE CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 507.8 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 375.6 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu Shielded Close enquire Close search Search AUT website Search academics Website search Search Popular searches nursing business engineering psychology physiotherapy education"
