    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=USl6e": {
      "title": "Collections Senior Manager",
      "description": "Collections Senior Manager - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Collections Senior Manager Collections Senior Manager Lead a high-performing, capable team. Bring your ideas and enthusiasm to preparing the way for Collections work of the future. Fixed-term, full-time role (37.5 hours) based at AUT's City Campus. Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Te Mātāpuna Library and Learning Services is AUT's whare pukapuka (library) and knowledge source. Our name recognises the special connection AUT has to the underground waterways and rivers that flow through Tāmaki Makaurau. Our mātāpuna (campus libraries) and services are foundational for Knowledge That Works . Te Mātāpuna teams are knowledge connectors and amplifiers, navigators, partners and kaitiaki. We centre our work around principles of openness, inclusivity and equity. As active Tiriti partners, we embed AUT’s Tiriti framework throughout our services. Our teams partner with the AUT community to lift academic skills and provide access to knowledge. We create learning opportunities and resources to raise achievement, research visibility and impact and to support open research and Māori and indigenous data sovereignty. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi This is an exceptional development opportunity to lead the Collections team, including contributing to the strategic direction of both the team and Te Mātāpuna Library & Learning Services. You will be leading a high performing and capable team. We are looking for someone with bold ideas and courage to try new things in a supportive environment. You will have the opportunity to shape the future of Collections work and its place in the new Te Mātāpuna 5 year plan. You will: embrace AUT's responsibility under Te Tiriti o Waitangi through the Te Aronui framework and its enactments of whakaea, whakaawe, whakamana and whakanui, re-imagine our collections strategy and work practices to enact kaitiakitanga, manaakitanga and whakawhanaungatanga, recognise the importance of open access in resource provision and contribute to strengthening our role in this area, bring a realistic, ethical and pragmatic perspective on the use of AI in collections work, be open to new ways of working, be collaborative and thrive in a learning environment. This role reports to and works closely with the Director Collections & Infrastructure, and is part of the Library Leadership Team. This is a full-time position, and is fixed-term due to parental leave. You will be based at our Waihorotiu (City) Campus but may need to work at our other campuses from time to time. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits . https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi , Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: a recognised postgraduate qualification preferably in MLIS/MIS. 7-8 years’ experience in a relevant professional library position. Knowledge of collections work, scholarly publishing and communications, and issues and trends in academic libraries. A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: dependent on candidate’s notice period, if applicable Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $110,000 - $131,000 per annum (dependent on experience and qualifications) For further information : please send us an enquiry or call 09 921 9499 Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 21 September 2026, 11:55pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96453 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96453 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Fixed term Closes on 21 Sep 2026 23:55 Expertise Library Experience level (s) Management More details (document) PD 1790 - Collections Senior Manager.pdf Posted on 03 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=s028e": {
      "title": "Employment Relations Advisor",
      "description": "Employment Relations Advisor - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Employment Relations Advisor Employment Relations Advisor Build your employment relations expertise in a diverse, complex environment, with opportunities to develop your skills and make a meaningful impact. Build trusted relationships and collaborate effectively to achieve positive outcomes. Permanent, full-time role based at AUT’s city campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. People and Culture is a strategic enabler of AUT’s mission, partnering across the University to build a high-performing, inclusive and future-focused workforce. We lift organisational performance through workforce strategy, strong leadership practices and a people experience that helps AUT’s strategy land. Guided by our People Plan, we build future capability by enabling people to thrive, strengthening belonging, and bringing our culture and values to life in everything we do. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We're passionate about creating positive workplace experiences and supporting our people to thrive. As our Employment Relations Advisor, you'll provide expert advice and support across a broad range of employment matters while building your experience in workplace investigations, collective bargaining, union engagement and policy development within a large and diverse organisation. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff. About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi , Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. You are a resilient and pragmatic professional who can confidently navigate sensitive and complex workplace situations. You bring sound judgement, emotional intelligence and empathy to your work, building trusted relationships and collaborating effectively to achieve positive outcomes. You are proactive, highly organised and solutions-focused, with a genuine interest in employment relations and a commitment to continuing to develop your expertise in this area. To be successful in this role, you will have: At least three years' experience in Human Resources or a related field. A relevant tertiary qualification in Human Resources, Employment Relations, Business, Psychology or a related discipline. Experience supporting employment relations matters in a complex environment. Sound knowledge of New Zealand employment legislation and employment relations principles. Experience supporting investigations, disciplinary processes, grievances, dispute resolution or mediation activities. Strong communication, relationship management and stakeholder engagement skills. Excellent analytical, research and report-writing capabilities. The ability to manage competing priorities while maintaining a high level of accuracy and professionalism. A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: To be agreed with the successful candidate. Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $76,000 - $102,000 commensurate with the skills and experience of the successful candidate. For further information : Contact Caroline Cranston, AUT Recruitment Consultant - caroline.cranston@aut.ac.nz Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 16 September 2026 Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96618 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96618 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 16 Sep 2026 17:00 Expertise Human Resources Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 40 - Employment Relations Advisor.pdf Posted on 02 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
