    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=vHx7e": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant",
      "description": "Teaching Assistant - UniPrep Uni101 - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Teaching Assistant - UniPrep Uni101 Teaching Assistant - UniPrep Uni101 Make a difference by teaching and mentoring a whānau group of up to 25 ākonga as they begin their university journey. Create a culturally rich and inspiring learning environment grounded in manaakitanga, whanaungatanga, and kaitiakitanga. Casual, hourly paid appointment based at AUT's South Campus during the summer. Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi AUT is excited to announce that we are recruiting Teaching Assistants (TAs) for UniPrep/Uni 101 2027 at AUT’s South Campus! The role is intended to run from 11 January to 19 February 2027, requiring approximately 26 hours per week. TAs will also be invited to two-days of whakawhanaungatanga in early December 2026 to meet the entire UniPrep programme team. Teaching Assistants will be responsible for teaching and mentoring a whānau group of 25 ākonga – high school leavers, primarily Māori and Pacific from the Tāmaki Makaurau region, who are beginning their university journey. TAs will foster a culturally affirming and inspiring learning environment that: Honours Te Tiriti o Waitangi and Te Aronui (AUT's Te Tiriti framework), while centring knowledge and practice from across Te Moana-nui-a-Kiwa. Supports a sense of belonging, wellbeing, and academic confidence for ākonga as they transition into university life. This role requires the successful delivery of culturally enriching tutorials using the material prepared for UniPrep/Uni101 under the mentorship of Dr. Jessica Worchel, the Uni101 Course Lead. TAs are responsible for ensuring students are clearly aware of learning outcomes and assessment requirements and are meeting the requirements of the paper as well as mentoring students on their academic journey through the creation of a university transition success plan. About you | Ko wai koe The ideal candidate will possess a service leadership mindset with effective organisational and communications skills and a strong ability to create a culturally rich and inspiring teaching and learning environment. They will have strong collaboration skills and be committed to working as a team with all UniPrep staff to support ākonga wellbeing and success. They will be grounded in an approach to work that is cultural, relational, and people-centred, and embraces manaakitanga, whanaungatanga, and kaitiakitanga. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT, you’ll be part of a values-led university that supports you to thrive in your academic career. Benefit from flexible working, a supportive culture, cultural capability development for all staff, and strong growth opportunities. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV: please submit a) a cover letter which explains why this particular role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) a statement addressing how you feel you meet some, or all, of the criteria above. All applications must be submitted through the online application process. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $38.21 per hour For academic enquiries: Contact Dr. Jessica Worchel at Jessica.worchel@aut.ac.nz For recruitment enquiries: Please send us an enquiry here or call 09 921 9499 Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96565 Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 22 September 2026, 11:55 pm This role is considered a children’s worker role and will be subject to safety checking as part of the Children’s Act 2014 At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96565 Location (s) South Campus Employment type (s) Casual (hourly paid) Closes on 22 Sep 2026 23:55 Expertise Academic, Academic Management, Adjunct Professor, Associate Professor, Clinical Educator, Lecturer, Midwife, Professor, Research, Senior Lecturer, Teaching Assistant Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) Posted on 01 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
