    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=ARU5e": {
      "title": "HR Coordinator",
      "description": "HR Coordinator - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies HR Coordinator HR Coordinator Bring your can-do attitude, knowledge, passion, and ideas Opportunity to grow your career Full-time, permanent based at our City Campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is bold and unapologetically different, centred on students and grounded in Knowledge that Works driven by talented, progressive people. We are New Zealand’s newest university, ranked 5-stars by QS Universities 2025 and a place of opportunity where more than 26,000 students with talent and potential succeed, supported by a community of more than 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. Built on collaboration, shared purpose and the values of Pono (fact, truth, reality, integrity), Tika (acting accordingly, doing what is needed, ethical expression), and Aroha (empathy, care, compassion). AUT offers an innovative, forward-thinking environment where committed people work together to improve outcomes for students, communities, and the world. AUT recognises the importance of Te Tiriti , Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership, and contribution across our university and is committed to creating environments where these communities can thrive. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. People and Culture is a strategic enabler of AUT’s mission, partnering across the University to build a high-performing, inclusive and future-focused workforce. We lift organisational performance through workforce strategy, strong leadership practices, and a people experience that helps AUT’s strategy land. Guided by our People Plan, we build future capability by enabling people to thrive, strengthening belonging, and bringing our culture and values to life in everything we do. Our team supports over 3,000 staff, growing to 4,000 at peak times across the academic year. There is never a dull moment! The O pportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi Reporting to the Operations Manager - Shared Services, you will provide first-line support for all aspects of HR administration during the employee lifecycle, from recruitment through to resignation. This is a highly active position suited to someone who enjoys staying busy and managing competing priorities. Your tasks will include answering first-level enquiries, keeping our intranet up to date, managing the organisation’s hierarchy/positions, and preparing changes to terms and conditions. You will also support our colleagues' administrative needs across People & Culture to ensure we deliver an outstanding HR experience.  This is an exciting opportunity for someone wanting to grow their career in HR in a supportive and encouraging environment. About you | Ko wai koe If you’re the kind of person who isn’t afraid to try new things, explore bold ideas and inject real energy and passion into the entire university experience, you’ll fit right in. To be successful in this role, you will have: Skills and Experience A team player with a strong work ethic who is quick to learn new systems and processes Strong administration skills with the ability to work under pressure, managing multiple tasks to meet tight deadlines Excellent written and verbal communication skillswith accuracy and attention to detail A customer service approach to your work and contribute positively to AUT’s culture Working knowledge of Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, Outlook) High level of confidentiality for sensitive information A commitment to equity , diversity and inclusion . Supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey ( https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/maori/auts-commitment-to-Te-Tiriti-o-Waitangi ). As a professional member of staff at AUT, you’ll help keep us moving forward. From improving our services and streamlining our systems to supporting the experiences of students and staff across our campuses. By working collaboratively, solving problems and driving practical improvements, you’ll play a vital role in helping us operate smoothly, raise our profile, and evolve what we do every day. You will bring an open, engaging, and collaborative approach, with the flexibility to respond to changing requirements, and actively contribute to a positive and collegial environment. You will demonstrate cultural humility, awareness, and respect when engaging with indigenous peoples and culturally diverse communities. Experience supporting indigenous, equity, or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly desirable. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT, you’ll be part of a values-led university that supports you to thrive in your role and career. We offer: Great opportunity to build on your HR skills and experience Working with a great team who are very supportive and fun Opportunities to be part of the process improvements and projects that are continuously happening Ongoing support and training opportunities for personal and professional development Being part of a department that is inclusive and wants you to succeed How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please ensure to submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please feel free to add any further comments you feel may also support your application. All applications must be submitted through the online application process. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: Following the selection of the successful candidate Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $62,000 - $81,000 per annum (dependent on experience and qualifications) For further information , please send us an enquiry here or call 09 921 9499 . (recruiters’ option to replace with their name here for ROC-led roles) Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 14th September 2026, at 11:55 pm. Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96431 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96431 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 14 Sep 2026 23:55 Expertise Human Resources Experience level (s) Experienced (Less than 2 years), Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 67 - HR Co-ordinator -.pdf Posted on 28 Aug 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/diversity-working-at-aut": {
      "title": "Embracing diversity and inclusion in the workplace",
      "description": "Embracing diversity and inclusion in the workplace - AUT We value your privacy We use cookies to enhance your browsing experience, enable features like live chat and embedded media, serve personalised ads and content, and understand how our website is used. By clicking “Accept All”, you consent to our use of cookies. Cookie Policy Customise Reject All Accept All Customise Consent Preferences We use cookies to help you navigate efficiently and perform certain functions. You will find detailed information about all cookies under each consent category below. The cookies that are categorised as \"Necessary\" are stored on your browser as they are essential for enabling the basic functionalities of the site. ... Show more For more information on how Google's third-party cookies operate and handle your data, see: Google Privacy Policy Necessary Always Active Necessary cookies are required to enable the basic features of this site, such as providing secure log-in or adjusting your consent preferences. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable data. Cookie dxp-sessionid Duration 1 hour Description Maintains the user's session within the Squiz DXP platform. Required for navigation, form interactions, and core site functionality. Cookie SQ_SYSTEM_SESSION Duration session Description Session cookie used by the Squiz CMS to track authenticated sessions and preserve user state across pages. Essential for system functions such as logins and editing tools. Cookie __cf_bm Duration 1 hour Description This cookie, set by Cloudflare, is used to support Cloudflare Bot Management. Cookie li_gc Duration 6 months Description Linkedin set this cookie for storing visitor's consent regarding using cookies for non-essential purposes. Cookie AWSALBCORS Duration 7 days Description Amazon Web Services set this cookie for load balancing. Cookie cookieyes-consent Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description CookieYes sets this cookie to remember users' consent preferences so that their preferences are respected on subsequent visits to this site. It does not collect or store any personal information about the site visitors. Functional Functional cookies help perform certain functionalities like sharing the content of the website on social media platforms, collecting feedback, and other third-party features. Cookie theme Duration session Description This cookie is used to set the colour theme of the website. Cookie lidc Duration 1 day Description LinkedIn sets the lidc cookie to facilitate data center selection. Analytics Analytical cookies are used to understand how visitors interact with the website. These cookies help provide information on metrics such as the number of visitors, bounce rate, traffic source, etc. Cookie gtm-session-start Duration 1 hour Description Records the start time of a user session for Google Tag Manager. Used to help measure website usage and session duration. Cookie _ga Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to calculate visitor, session and campaign data and track site usage for the site's analytics report. The cookie stores information anonymously and assigns a randomly generated number to recognise unique visitors. Cookie _gid Duration 1 day Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store information on how visitors use a website while also creating an analytics report of the website's performance. Some of the collected data includes the number of visitors, their source, and the pages they visit anonymously. Cookie _gat_UA-* Duration 1 minute Description Google Analytics sets this cookie for user behaviour tracking. Cookie _ga_* Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store and count page views. Cookie _hjSessionUser_* Duration 1 year Description Hotjar sets this cookie to ensure data from subsequent visits to the same site is attributed to the same user ID, which persists in the Hotjar User ID, which is unique to that site. Cookie _hjSession_* Duration 1 hour Description Hotjar sets this cookie to ensure data from subsequent visits to the same site is attributed to the same user ID, which persists in the Hotjar User ID, which is unique to that site. Cookie _twpid Duration 1 year 24 days Description This cookie is set by Tealium to assign a unique, anonymous identifier to each visitor. It allows the platform to recognise the same user across different sessions and domains to provide a consistent experience, support visitor stitching for unified profiles, and generate accurate website usage statistics. Performance Performance cookies are used to understand and analyse the key performance indexes of the website which helps in delivering a better user experience for the visitors. Cookie AWSALB Duration 7 days Description AWSALB is an application load balancer cookie set by Amazon Web Services to map the session to the target. Advertisement Advertisement cookies are used to provide visitors with customised advertisements based on the pages you visited previously and to analyse the effectiveness of the ad campaigns. Cookie ttcsid_C5N07UH1P6O5QGAPR6KG Duration 3 months Description TikTok Pixel session identifier used for analytics, ad attribution, and measuring campaign performance. Cookie ttcsid Duration 3 months Description Tracks user behaviour for TikTok advertising, enabling ad performance measurement and personalised marketing. Cookie pageviewCount Duration session Description This cookie is used for determining the number of pages visited by a visitor on the website. It is used for marketing purposes. Cookie _ttp Duration 3 months Description TikTok set this cookie to track and improve the performance of advertising campaigns, as well as to personalise the user experience. Cookie muc_ads Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Twitter sets this cookie to collect user behaviour and interaction data to optimize the website. Cookie personalization_id Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Twitter sets this cookie to integrate and share features for social media and also store information about how the user uses the website, for tracking and targeting. Cookie _mkto_trk Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description This cookie, provided by Marketo, has information (such as a unique user ID) that is used to track the user's site usage. The cookies set by Marketo are readable only by Marketo. Cookie bcookie Duration 1 year Description LinkedIn sets this cookie from LinkedIn share buttons and ad tags to recognize browser IDs. Cookie _tt_enable_cookie Duration 3 months Description Tiktok set this cookie to collect data about behaviour and activities on the website and to measure the effectiveness of the advertising. Cookie _gcl_au Duration 3 months Description Google Tag Manager sets this cookie to experiment advertisement efficiency of websites using their services. Uncategorised Other uncategorised cookies are those that are being analysed and have not been classified into a category as yet. No cookies to display. Reject All Save My Preferences Accept All Skip to Content Skip to Main navigation Top bar navigation Students Staff Alumni Enquire Apply Website search Main navigation AUT Website search Toggle navigation Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Enquire Apply Students Staff Alumni Ako Study Ako Study Ready to plan for a future you're confident about? Explore programmes that lead to real careers, find your perfect fit and make your next move count. Find out more Study options Why study at AUT? Applying Entry requirements Fees and scholarships Changing my enrolment Information for high school students Information for career advisors Information for parents and whānau Information for adult learners Semester dates University that works differently Why study at AUT? See why we do things differently here at AUT and what that means for your learning. Learn more Tāwāhi International Tāwāhi International Thinking of studying in New Zealand? See why students from over 140 countries choose AUT for modern learning experiences that prepare you for success. Find out more Study options for international students Why study at AUT as an international student Scholarships for international students International student support Check before you come to New Zealand Meet AUT in your country International agents Contact us AUT International Office AUT China Website - 奥克兰理工大学中文官方网站 Scholarships for international students International student support Worried about the cost of studying in New Zealand? There's funding available – and you might qualify. Learn more Oranga Tauira Student Life Oranga Tauira Student Life We've got your back from day one. Discover all the support and experiences that help you feel at home and make the most of every uni moment. Find out more New students Around campus Accommodation Studying & IT Support services Student health and wellbeing Opportunities & careers Graduation Life in Auckland AUTSA - AUT student association We've got your back Financial services and support for students Facing financial challenges? We're here to help with essential support when you need it most. Learn more Rangahau Research Rangahau Research Problems that keep communities up at night? We're working on those. Explore research that creates solutions for real-world challenges that matter well beyond the university. Find out more Research networks, institutes and centres AUT Ventures (research commercialisation) Research and development services Participate in AUT research Research Week AUT Research Office Faculty postgraduate contacts Academic departments Graduate Research School Postgraduate research student support Postgraduate study options Research ethics Research that matters Research networks, institutes and centres From AI to public health, our research networks, institutes and centres work on problems that really matter. Learn more Ngātahi Partnerships Ngātahi Partnerships Ready to solve problems together? Discover how we partner with industry, community and government to tackle real challenges and drive meaningful change together. Learn  more Employ a student or graduate: find AUT talent for your business Research and development services Promote your business on campus: employer and industry events Use AUT's research facilities and equipment AUT Ventures (research commercialisation) Auckland FC partnership Community that cares Student Support Fund When students need support, our community steps up. See how you can help make a difference. Learn more Mō Mātou About Mō Mātou About Curious about AUT? Get to know our story, meet our leadership and find out what makes us different as a top modern university. Find out more AUT’s leadership Faculties and schools Campuses and locations Teaching, learning and assessment AUT rankings AUT awards and honours AI at AUT Sustainability Disability Action Plan Māori at AUT Pacific at AUT Working at AUT AUT values Our facilities Check a graduate’s qualification AUT Impact Policy hub History of AUT Contact AUT Apply Website search Home About Working at AUT Embracing diversity and inclusion in the workplace Embracing diversity and inclusion in the workplace Browse jobs Get job alerts More than half of AUT's staff were born overseas, in 118 different countries. They bring different backgrounds, identities, cultures and perspectives – and that shapes everything about how we work, teach and research. It's what makes our university what it is. We back that up with real commitments: staff networks built by the people themselves, development programmes that build cultural capability, and a track record of firsts in workplace inclusion across Aotearoa New Zealand and beyond. Leading on diversity and inclusion AUT has achieved several New Zealand and world firsts in workplace diversity and inclusion. These aren't badges we collect; they're commitments that shape how we work every day. Supporting Māori and Pacific staff AUT launched the Eke Tangaroa programme – the first of its kind – creating pathways for new Māori and Pacific academic staff in teaching and research. We aspire to be the university of choice for Māori and Pacific communities Advancing gender equity AUT is the first university to receive the Advanced GenderTick accreditation – recognition of sustained, practical commitment to gender equality in the workplace. Building a hearing-aware workplace Through the Hearing Accredited Workplace Programme (HAWP) our whole community has the tools and training to support staff and students who are Deaf or hard of hearing. Championing rainbow inclusion AUT was New Zealand’s first Rainbow-friendly university. We've taken the Pride Pledge , established the Rainbow Staff Network, appointed a full-time Student Inclusion Manager (Rainbow) and launched Ia, the world's first Rainbow research e-portal . Supporting hidden disabilities Our Hidden Disabilities Sunflower Lanyard Programme means staff and students with non-apparent disabilities can choose to be visible in a way that works for them. Supporting menopause at work AUT has partnered with Nest Consulting on peri/menopause support – recognising the impact of this life stage on our people and building a workplace where everyone can do their best work. Staff networks Our staff networks are voluntary and employee-led – built around shared identities, backgrounds and interests, and open to anyone who wants to be part of them. Our staff networks include: Cultural affinity groups: bringing together staff from Asian, African, Māori and Pacific communities through our African Staff Friendship Network, Asian Staff Network, Ngā Whānau Māori and Pacific Staff Network OUT@AUT: connecting and supporting staff and allies of rainbow communities Access Inclusion Network: supporting staff with lived experiences of physical and hidden disabilities, members of the Deaf community and others with access needs Women on Campus: providing formal and informal support for women at AUT and addressing issues that affect women within the university Parents @AUT: peer support for working parents navigating their parenting journey Together, our people are the threads that give strength and colour to our collective whāriki (woven mat); woven together through shared purpose, values and relationships.\" The diversity and progressiveness of AUT really stood out to me – acknowledging birthdays and having social activities that our social committee puts on. I’ve found true allies here. I’ve been able to build authentic relationships with people willing to listen, support, learn alongside me and help create change together. Brody Manase Videographer, Brand and Marketing Services Tash Puketapu Kaiurungi, People & Culture Previous Next Learn from what we teach AUT teaches the skills and knowledge that build inclusive communities, and our staff have access to that same expertise. Programmes available to all staff include: New Zealand Sign Language courses Te Reo Māori language courses Māori and indigenous development programmes Honouring Te Tiriti o Waitangi Our commitment to Te Tiriti o Waitangi is guided by Te Aronui, AUT's Te Tiriti Framework – shaping how we act, lead and work together. Aronui Ora, our professional development programme, helps staff engage with Te Aronui with confidence and understanding. HONOURING TE TIRITI O WAITANGI Our values Three values are at the heart of everything AUT does: pono, tika and aroha. They ground us in truth and shape every decision we make. Our values are the foundation our university is built on. Find out what that looks like in practice. AUT VALUES CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 507.8 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 375.6 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu Shielded Close enquire Close search Search AUT website Search academics Website search Search Popular searches nursing business engineering psychology physiotherapy education"
    }
  },
